<title>FRANCE: SGS-Thomson falls after results.</title>
<headline>SGS-Thomson falls after results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in SGS-Thomson fell more steeply than the market on Monday after the semiconductor company reported a drop in first-quarter net income to $90.50 million from $175 million.</p>
<p>The stock was down 4.46 percent at 375.30 francs at 0930 GMT. The CAC-40 index was down 0.9 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The results were pretty terrible,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>SGS-Thomson said the results reflected price erosion. It said sales dropped to $944.90 million from $1.03 billion in the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
